{"term":"arbitrary","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:2bdda49536af0b4823","definition":"Based on individual discretion or judgment; not based on any objective distinction, perhaps even made at random.","example":"Benjamin Franklin's designation of \"positive\" and \"negative\" to different charges was arbitrary.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"usually","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1489282e3463b839ae","definition":"Determined by impulse rather than reason; often connoting heavy-handedness.","example":"1937/1938, Albert Einstein, letter to Max Born\nThe Russian trials were Stalin's purges, with which he attempted to consolidate his power. Like most people in the West, I believed these show trials to be the arbitrary acts of a cruel dictator.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:529b37dc1136b96413","definition":"Any, out of all that are possible.","example":"The equation is true for an arbitrary value of x.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c95a6fd9b0b84c3e7b","definition":"Determined by independent arbiter.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35a64746e8416371da","definition":"Not representative or symbolic; not iconic.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f2ca5ae55ea857e66","definition":"Anything arbitrary, such as an arithmetical value or a fee.","example":"And in this long chain of consistence, a chain stretching from the long dead to the far unborn, the notion of the arbitrary could only survive as the notion of a pre-established arbitrary.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbitrary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈɑː.bɪ.tɹə.ɹi/"},"wordFamily":["arbitrarily","arbitrariness","arbitrarity","arbitrary-precision arithmetic","arbitrary unit","nonarbitrary","unarbitrary"]}